{"meta":{"ticker":"IJH","as_of_date":"2026-06-30","performance_as_of":"2026-06-30","generated_at":"2026-07-01 08:23:25"},"benchmark":{"ticker":"SPY","fund_name":"State Street SPDR S&P 500 ETF"},"overview":{"ticker":"IJH","fund_name":"iShares Core S&P Mid-Cap ETF","category":"US Mid-Cap Blend","issuer":"BlackRock","index_name":"S&P Mid Cap 400","region":"North America","exchange":"NYSEARCA","expense_ratio":0.0005,"aum":118499429961,"holdings_count":408,"inception_date":"2000-05-22","overall_score":8.85400673433363,"overall_rank":69,"sector_diversification_score":7.01255129616655},"description":{"tsi_description":"IJH is a mid-cap equity ETF that tracks the S&P MidCap 400 Index and provides diversified exposure to U.S. companies positioned between the large- and small-cap segments. The Index applies a profitability requirement for new constituents, which helps maintain stronger quality characteristics than many small-cap benchmarks. Compared to large-cap ETFs, IJH typically offers lower valuation multiples and reduced concentration risk, while maintaining stronger profitability and earnings growth characteristics than many small-cap peers. Its broad diversification and balanced sector exposure have historically positioned it as a middle ground between the growth-oriented large-cap market and the more volatile small-cap segment. Overall, IJH offers a balanced and diversified approach to mid-cap investing.","strategy_steps":["Tracks the S&P MidCap 400 Index.","Selects companies ranked approximately #501-900 by market capitalization from the S&P 1500 Composite Index.","Applies a profitability requirement for new Index entrants.","Uses a committee-managed selection process rather than purely rules-based market-cap ranking.","Includes approximately 400 holdings.","Uses a float-adjusted market-capitalization weighting methodology.","Maintains broad diversification with relatively low concentration among top holdings.","Rebalances quarterly."],"best_for":["Mid-cap exposure",